=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: A script that builds, called from the same place, is production evidence, refused for a weakened assertion (D-199)
d199: D-199 (0.12) refuses repair evidence for this rule. The inputs are unchanged; they were the case runner_one_hop_build_neg, held at warn by that evidence. REPAIR_EVIDENCE_REFUSED pins that the production change still reached the finding.
origin: FP guard — one hop must terminate in a test runner, or every build script becomes ci
=== head: scripts/compile.sh ===
#!/bin/sh -e
cc -O2 -shared -o libfast.so fast.c
=== before: scripts/ci.sh ===
#!/bin/sh -e
./scripts/compile.sh
=== after: scripts/ci.sh ===
#!/bin/sh -e
./scripts/compile.sh || true
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) == 105.0
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from billing import invoice_total


def test_total():
    assert invoice_total([50.0, 50.0], 0.05) > 0
